#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186564751 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3db48d91-b4ae-5bc4-9e23-cf8f6e4f61e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{y^{3}}{3} + 2 y=x^{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564741} {:answer/id #uuid "6206b0ac-0af8-5a3f-bdb6-4d8a7d7ca857" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{y^{3}}{3} + 2 y=x^{3} + 2 x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564750} {:answer/id #uuid "ad5dda92-fb69-524e-9ed8-013a6fcc7fa4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{y^{3}}{3} + 2 y=- x^{3} - 2 x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564775} {:answer/id #uuid "e5c81e6d-90b3-532e-917c-fc396c72ed2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{y^{3}}{3} + 2 y=2 x^{3} + 4 x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564788} {:answer/id #uuid "e8165d18-a888-5e20-a4c0-b83a0d45a046" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{y^{3}}{3}=x^{3} + 2 x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564790}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186564750} :answer-field/id #uuid "ab9169ec-e614-5c1c-b802-0f7689147026" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564773}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "67842345-f981-5889-9968-724d74a791f4" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) $$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{3 x^{2} + 2}{y^{2} + 2}.\n$$" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{3 x^{2} + 2}{y^{2} + 2} \\\\ (y^{2} + 2)\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =3 x^{2} + 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (y^{2} + 2)\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (3 x^{2} + 2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (y^{2} + 2)\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int (3 x^{2} + 2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (y^{2} + 2)\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (3 x^{2} + 2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int y^2\\,\\text{d}y+\\int 2\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int 3x^2\\,\\text{d}x+\\int 2\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{y^3}{3}+2y & =\\frac{3x^3}{3}+2x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\frac{y^{3}}{3} + 2 y=x^{3} + 2 x+C.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186564765 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f8484bf-64ea-5867-960d-dcaa3c1c31cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{y^{3}}{3}=2 x^{3} - 2 x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564742} {:answer/id #uuid "693e1877-dfd3-5001-ba07-145a54c04108" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{y^{3}}{3}=x^{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564753} {:answer/id #uuid "81face9a-ba0e-55ba-aaf6-2789ea3fc77a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{y^{3}}{3}=x^{3} - x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564763} {:answer/id #uuid "da88f524-d602-526c-8270-14433512acbb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{y^{3}}{3}=- x^{3} + x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564785} {:answer/id #uuid "fad7d945-449c-53cd-84b3-c9526c957dce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y^{2}=x^{3} - x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564792}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186564763} :answer-field/id #uuid "ff14abc5-d173-5b95-a42b-0fc4a6a416f2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564795}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "86c62ee5-0b3a-5e0d-80cf-01bdae5b5c10" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) $$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{3 x^{2} - 1}{y^{2}}.\n$$ Work on an interval where $y\\ne 0.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{3 x^{2} - 1}{y^{2}} \\\\ (y^{2})\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =3 x^{2} - 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (y^{2})\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (3 x^{2} - 1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (y^{2})\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int (3 x^{2} - 1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (y^{2})\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (3 x^{2} - 1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int y^2\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int 3x^2\\,\\text{d}x-\\int 1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{y^3}{3} & =\\frac{3x^3}{3}-1x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\frac{y^{3}}{3}=x^{3} - x+C.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186564766 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14279e6e-5311-594c-94e9-2104eba29b1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{y^{3}}{3} + y=\\frac{5 x^{3}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564731} {:answer/id #uuid "350cacb7-df00-5ad5-a272-e0602f516b58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{y^{3}}{3} + y=- \\frac{5 x^{3}}{3} - x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564737} {:answer/id #uuid "5d5dc513-5a6c-5372-9b20-204a745764b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{y^{3}}{3} + y=\\frac{10 x^{3}}{3} + 2 x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564747} {:answer/id #uuid "9d113a1b-0954-5b3f-a454-fc359a3dc2a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{y^{3}}{3}=\\frac{5 x^{3}}{3} + x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564771} {:answer/id #uuid "d76c06a6-e0ab-5880-9cf9-88e14247f150" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{y^{3}}{3} + y=\\frac{5 x^{3}}{3} + x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564783}] :answer-field/correc