& =\\int (3 x^{2} - 2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (y^{2} + 1)\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (3 x^{2} - 2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int y^2\\,\\text{d}y+\\int 1\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int 3x^2\\,\\text{d}x-\\int 2\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{y^3}{3}+1y & =\\frac{3x^3}{3}-2x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\frac{y^{3}}{3} + y=x^{3} - 2 x+C.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186564776 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f40e511-9162-550c-9ca2-45069c532860" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{y^{3}}{3} + 2 y=\\frac{2 x^{3}}{3} - 4 x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564728} {:answer/id #uuid "5e5b365d-b010-5d40-ae9b-7cdf2bc9fef7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{y^{3}}{3} + 2 y=\\frac{4 x^{3}}{3} - 8 x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564748} {:answer/id #uuid "5e654d84-87a6-5c4a-b50f-52951169e736" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{y^{3}}{3} + 2 y=- \\frac{2 x^{3}}{3} + 4 x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564749} {:answer/id #uuid "928f0b31-f944-5f57-a0b8-e69268c93db4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{y^{3}}{3}=\\frac{2 x^{3}}{3} - 4 x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564767} {:answer/id #uuid "d900b285-6248-5c1b-87a5-f18bdbb83a2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{y^{3}}{3} + 2 y=\\frac{2 x^{3}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564784}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186564728} :answer-field/id #uuid "813d9f9a-fa68-5dc1-9e51-8ed9878f3c04" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564762}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "b65718d4-b12a-5895-93fb-8677bffa9b3c" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) $$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2 x^{2} - 4}{y^{2} + 2}.\n$$" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{2 x^{2} - 4}{y^{2} + 2} \\\\ (y^{2} + 2)\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2 x^{2} - 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (y^{2} + 2)\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (2 x^{2} - 4)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (y^{2} + 2)\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int (2 x^{2} - 4)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (y^{2} + 2)\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (2 x^{2} - 4)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int y^2\\,\\text{d}y+\\int 2\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int 2x^2\\,\\text{d}x-\\int 4\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{y^3}{3}+2y & =\\frac{2x^3}{3}-4x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\frac{y^{3}}{3} + 2 y=\\frac{2 x^{3}}{3} - 4 x+C.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186564781 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a80263b-0173-50c1-8dde-6c3cfba6f1ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{y^{3}}{3}=- \\frac{2 x^{3}}{3} + 4 x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564733} {:answer/id #uuid "43098fc8-a701-552a-8369-84c5e4b393e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{y^{3}}{3}=\\frac{4 x^{3}}{3} - 8 x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564743} {:answer/id #uuid "9672fd10-89cb-571c-8f61-a39749abc788" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y^{2}=\\frac{2 x^{3}}{3} - 4 x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564768} {:answer/id #uuid "cccfbb02-c9ff-5a31-8add-f1c2e35d57c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{y^{3}}{3}=\\frac{2 x^{3}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564782} {:answer/id #uuid "e62dc35a-2c8a-5355-936e-f363e3f97dcb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{y^{3}}{3}=\\frac{2 x^{3}}{3} - 4 x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564789}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186564789} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a317931-280d-5d7f-9352-0a157680e251" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564770}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "c08898da-32ad-5a3c-a964-0cd90dc6de56" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) $$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2 x^{2} - 4}{y^{2}}.\n$$ Work on an interval where $y\\ne 0.$" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{2 x^{2} - 4}{y^{2}} \\\\ (y^{2})\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2 x^{2} - 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (y^{2})\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (2 x^{2} - 4)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (y^{2})\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int (2 x^{2} - 4)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (y^{2})\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (2 x^{2} - 4)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int y^2\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int 2x^2\\,\\text{d}x-\\int 4\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{y^3}{3} & =\\frac{2x^3}{3}-4x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\frac{y^{3}}{3}=\\frac{2 x^{3}}{3} - 4 x+C.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186564787 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3414c5d2-20cf-5914-a9a9-332d71670cb0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{y^{3}}{3}=x^{3} - 2 x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564736} {:answer/id #uuid "397ebe0f-f377-53d2-bd21-fce260323bf0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{y^{3}}{3}=x^{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564739} {:answer/id #uuid "6894bf98-eb66-522e-979d-33a00c26d36b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{y^{3}}{3}=- x^{3} + 2 x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564752} {:answer/id #uuid "79ced1aa-6ded-5a07-87bd-71bc6d94480b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{y^{3}}{3}=2 x^{3} - 4 x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564759} {:answer/id #uuid "bb910cc9-69e7-5653-ace0-42a53998a788" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y^{2}=x^{3} - 2 x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564779}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186564736} :answer-field/id #uuid "6be49230-b2e0-5bf2-9f22-b2261d348685" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564754}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "e3a102d8-6b1a-53a5-a710-b6fa6cc5a594" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) $$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{3 x^{2} - 2}{y^{2}}.\n$$ Work on an interval where $y\\ne 0.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{3 x^{2} - 2}{y^{2}} \\\\ (y^{2})\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =3 x^{2} - 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (y^{2})\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (3 x^{2} - 2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (y^{2})\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int (3 x^{2} - 2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (y^{2})\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (3 x^{2} - 2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int y^2\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int 3x^2\\,\\text{d}x-\\int 2\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{y^3}{3} & =\\frac{3x^3}{3}-2x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\frac{y^{3}}{3}=x^{3} - 2 x+C.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186565593 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6fc5a380-1983-5fd3-a9a8-a3c2ecf287fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-4(3 - 4 x)^{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565591} {:answer/id #uuid "73f4128f-a1d8-5bf3-ad9f-85f70a222251" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3(3 - 4 x)^{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565592} {:answer/id #uuid "95a11de1-bb6b-5eb4-8e63-f0b053e1f1df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6(3 - 4 x)^{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565595} {:answer/id #uuid "c2fd3656-3e39-56a1-92a1-6955b83b3b0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-24(3 - 4 x)^{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565598} {:answer/id #uuid "f881b92f-d7fe-54ff-9a4d-3e96bd197db8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-24(3 - 4 x)^{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565603}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186565603} :answer-field/id #uuid "bad14dfb-e7b1-549d-8b87-2f1d672c7de0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565597}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "7a04edd0-e7bf-56e5-8b7e-72d1c5d80068" :question/problem "Find $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}$ when $f(x)=(3 - 4 x)^{6}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $f(x)$ as a composite function:\n\n$$\nf=g^{6},\\,g=3 - 4 x\n$$\n\nThe chain rule states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}=6g^{5},\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}=-4.\n$$\n\nFinally, multiplying the two together and substituting for $g$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} &=6g^{5}\\cdot (-4) \\\\  &=-24(3 - 4 x)^{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186565600 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "37815dd4-eb85-5506-a53b-02d708dc63b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "12x(-1+2x)^{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565590} {:answer/id #uuid "7ca845be-815d-54b6-b943-67a05dfc5659" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "16(-1+2x)^{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565594} {:answer/id #uuid "c4a651a1-21d4-5d6e-99e6-82d10932c207" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "12(-1+2x)^{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565599} {:answer/id #uuid "d0dc0981-4569-5cd4-81b4-a1e05d370b16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3(-1+2x)^{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565601} {:answer/id #uuid "f30538b4-9ca0-589f-b496-783cf99694de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6(-1+2x)^{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565602}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186565599} :answer-field/id #uuid "a28f42e5-36b6-5f5e-8b58-a45c3ea6040b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565596}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "c560bc6a-e1e6-5b7e-9d3d-86522a3c4ff0" :question/problem "Find $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}$ when $f(x)=(-1+2x)^{6}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $f(x)$ as a composite function:\n\n$$\nf=g^{6},\\,g=-1+2x\n$$\n\nThe chain rule states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}=6g^{5},\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}=2.\n$$\n\nFinally, multiplying the two together and substituting for $g$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} &=6\\cdot 2\\cdot (-1+2x)^{5} \\\\  &=12(-1+2x)^{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567154 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f3c17f1-f814-5b07-b43e-943e91349a7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=14x\\ln|x|+Cx^2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567155} {:answer/id #uuid "1ac7af4b-1410-5e5d-8017-81bae574ddb8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=7x\\ln|x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567158} {:answer/id #uuid "509ae4d5-c63f-5f05-948e-50319104d5bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=7\\ln|x|+Cx^2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567163} {:answer/id #uuid "5379b768-1beb-5eff-8735-b067756a5b5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=7\\ln|x|+Cx" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567164} {:answer/id #uuid "9d6edc00-118b-5935-bf52-4378edc2c1fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=7x\\ln|x|+Cx" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567179}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567179} :answer-field/id #uuid "037f8ee7-d7a4-57d7-a847-a86c53618745" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567153}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "044bf3fa-78d9-52d3-92f7-f8c3e8e8fe40" :question/problem "Use the transformation $y=v(x)x$ to find the general solution of the following homogeneous differential equation.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}=\\frac{7x+y}{x}\n$$" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "With $y=v(x)x$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}&=x\\frac{\\mathrm{d}v}{\\mathrm{d}x}+v\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}(x) \\\\ &=x\\frac{\\mathrm{d}v}{\\mathrm{d}x}+v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\frac{\\mathrm{d}v}{\\mathrm{d}x}+v&=\\frac{7x+(vx)}{x} \\\\ x\\frac{\\mathrm{d}v}{\\mathrm{d}x}+v&=7+v \\\\ x\\frac{\\mathrm{d}v}{\\mathrm{d}x}&=7 \\\\ \\frac{\\mathrm{d}v}{\\mathrm{d}x}&=\\frac{7}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating both sides with respect to $x$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int\\mathrm{d}v&=7\\int\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ v&=7\\ln|x|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the transformation $y=vx$, we get\n\n$$\nv=\\frac{y}{x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our solution, we finally obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y}{x}&=7\\ln|x|+C \\\\ y&=7x\\ln|x|+Cx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n\n\nThe solution is used on intervals where $x\\ne0$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567157 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8de07726-58f6-5f73-b863-f8afab4e1c8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=x\\sqrt{-2\\ln|x|+C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567174} {:answer/id #uuid "a1875a7a-51e4-5a07-9308-9735d0a1dde6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=x(-4\\ln|x|+C)^2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567181} {:answer/id #uuid "d8d0200b-aa5b-5a87-8ab2-2668e57d18fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=x(-6\\ln|x|+C)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567183} {:answer/id #uuid "e40fe086-141b-59ea-bb51-36d8df716744" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=x\\sqrt[3]{-6\\ln|x|+C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567185} {:answer/id #uuid "ee631a80-54cd-5f8e-9d1a-a43791010e05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=x^2(-6\\ln|x|+C)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567186}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567185} :answer-field/id #uuid "441e14d4-c75f-58ce-99d2-6eda7fa138a1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567162}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "14c59b9c-9898-5981-8eeb-e3c3847c9e85" :question/problem "Use the transformation $y=v(x)x$ to find the general solution of the following homogeneous differential equation.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}=\\frac{-2x^3+y^3}{xy^2}\n$$" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "With $y=v(x)x$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}&=x\\frac{\\mathrm{d}v}{\\mathrm{d}x}+v\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}(x) \\\\ &=x\\frac{\\mathrm{d}v}{\\mathrm{d}x}+v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\frac{\\mathrm{d}v}{\\mathrm{d}x}+v&=\\frac{-2x^3+(vx)^3}{x(vx)^2} \\\\ x\\frac{\\mathrm{d}v}{\\mathrm{d}x}+v&=\\frac{-2+v^3}{v^2}=\\frac{-2}{v^2}+v \\\\ x\\frac{\\mathrm{d}v}{\\mathrm{d}x}&=\\frac{-2}{v^2} \\\\ v^2\\frac{\\mathrm{d}v}{\\mathrm{d}x}&=\\frac{-2}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating both sides with respect to $x$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int v^2\\,\\mathrm{d}v&=-2\\int\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ \\frac{v^3}{3}&=-2\\ln|x|+C_1 \\\\ v^3&=-6\\ln|x|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the transformation $y=vx$, we get\n\n$$\nv=\\frac{y}{x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our solution, we finally obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left(\\frac{y}{x}\\right)^3&=-6\\ln|x|+C \\\\ y^3&=x^3(-6\\ln|x|+C) \\\\ y&=x\\sqrt[3]{-6\\ln|x|+C}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere $C=3C_1$ and the cube root is real. Restrict the solution to intervals where $y\\ne0$.\n\nThe solution is used on intervals where $x\\ne0$ and $y\\ne0$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567160 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14b066f4-4aed-54e4-ac8e-dda7e0de8355" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=x\\sqrt[3]{12\\ln|x|+C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567156} {:answer/id #uuid "1f2c49bd-7234-5991-b192-bafd8e3ae024" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=x\\sqrt{4\\ln|x|+C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567159} {:answer/id #uuid "7302a1d3-6f54-5755-b057-1f9a8eb5c77e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=x(8\\ln|x|+C)^2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567170} {:answer/id #uuid "9d1fa502-efec-5568-818f-b442c164f06f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=x(12\\ln|x|+C)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567178} {:answer/id #uuid "d3e8de7f-11cc-50d1-96ac-1a3238c95b38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=x^2(12\\ln|x|+C)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567182}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567156} :answer-field/id #uuid "95eba5e4-d1fe-5b11-ada8-85aabed1f8dc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567177}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "2575ad75-ecae-5053-bd6f-925ac6982583" :question/problem "Use the transformation $y=v(x)x$ to find the general solution of the following homogeneous differential equation.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}=\\frac{4x^3+y^3}{xy^2}\n$$" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "With $y=v(x)x$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}&=x\\frac{\\mathrm{d}v}{\\mathrm{d}x}+v\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}(x) \\\\ &=x\\frac{\\mathrm{d}v}{\\mathrm{d}x}+v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\frac{\\mathrm{d}v}{\\mathrm{d}x}+v&=\\frac{4x^3+(vx)^3}{x(vx)^2} \\\\ x\\frac{\\mathrm{d}v}{\\mathrm{d}x}+v&=\\frac{4+v^3}{v^2}=\\frac{4}{v^2}+v \\\\ x\\frac{\\mathrm{d}v}{\\mathrm{d}x}&=\\frac{4}{v^2} \\\\ v^2\\frac{\\mathrm{d}v}{\\mathrm{d}x}&=\\frac{4}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating both sides with respect to $x$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int v^2\\,\\mathrm{d}v&=4\\int\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ \\frac{v^3}{3}&=4\\ln|x|+C_1 \\\\ v^3&=12\\ln|x|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the transformation $y=vx$, we get\n\n$$\nv=\\frac{y}{x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our solution, we finally obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left(\\frac{y}{x}\\right)^3&=12\\ln|x|+C \\\\ y^3&=x^3(12\\ln|x|+C) \\\\ y&=x\\sqrt[3]{12\\ln|x|+C}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere $C=3C_1$ and the cube root is real. Restrict the solution to intervals where $y\\ne0$.\n\nThe solution is used on intervals where $x\\ne0$ and $y\\ne0$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567161 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5a54a25e-c2da-560f-944f-0aa251938d3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=-4\\ln|x|+Cx" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567166} {:answer/id #uuid "798be044-79ad-575c-9a9c-79ea53d43171" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=-4x\\ln|x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567171} {:answer/id #uuid "7be5f568-a6f3-513f-af44-19d3adcdf073" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=-8x\\ln|x|+Cx^2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567172} {:answer/id #uuid "91cb8bb6-c80a-5286-ba98-3a7085744f62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=-4\\ln|x|+Cx^2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567175} {:answer/id #uuid "a027748e-15f1-5e67-8fba-ccf0922fd80b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=-4x\\ln|x|+Cx" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567180}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567180} :answer-field/id #uuid "7097afc5-ccdc-5d12-8650-7ab04dfb6cc4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567169}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "42363691-301e-5615-be59-d0f1dea51b33" :question/problem "Use the transformation $y=v(x)x$ to find the general solution of the following homogeneous differential equation.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}=\\frac{-4x+y}{x}\n$$" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "With $y=v(x)x$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}&=x\\frac{\\mathrm{d}v}{\\mathrm{d}x}+v\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}(x) \\\\ &=x\\frac{\\mathrm{d}v}{\\mathrm{d}x}+v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\frac{\\mathrm{d}v}{\\mathrm{d}x}+v&=\\frac{-4x+(vx)}{x} \\\\ x\\frac{\\mathrm{d}v}{\\mathrm{d}x}+v&=-4+v \\\\ x\\frac{\\mathrm{d}v}{\\mathrm{d}x}&=-4 \\\\ \\frac{\\mathrm{d}v}{\\mathrm{d}x}&=\\frac{-4}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating both sides with respect to $x$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int\\mathrm{d}v&=-4\\int\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ v&=-4\\ln|x|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the transformation $y=vx$, we get\n\n$$\nv=\\frac{y}{x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our solution, we finally obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y}{x}&=-4\\ln|x|+C \\\\ y&=-4x\\ln|x|+Cx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n\n\nThe solution is used on intervals where $x\\ne0$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567173 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "011cc7e9-984a-5e87-9d00-e574f53f42be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=Cx^2-6x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567152} {:answer/id #uuid "69e6cea4-2f9f-5b0a-ab0c-77cd1fbc615c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=Cx^3+6x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567167} {:answer/id #uuid "6ac73021-fbb0-59bd-a82c-a377e9ceb430" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=Cx^3-6x^2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567168} {:answer/id #uuid "943a18de-d8dc-53f7-93bb-efbd8d79fcc0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=Cx^3-12x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567176} {:answer/id #uuid "e35b6663-8b09-584d-9cd8-c852a4db108b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=Cx^2+12x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567184}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567152} :answer-field/id #uuid "5839d98f-4e19-5d79-84da-c6787f331cd4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567165}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "8370ea02-6e2b-5cde-a685-02002fe09af6" :question/problem "Use the transformation $y=v(x)x$ to find the general solution of the following homogeneous differential equation.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}=\\frac{6x+2y}{x}\n$$" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "With $y=v(x)x$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}&=x\\frac{\\mathrm{d}v}{\\mathrm{d}x}+v\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}(x) \\\\ &=x\\frac{\\mathrm{d}v}{\\mathrm{d}x}+v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\frac{\\mathrm{d}v}{\\mathrm{d}x}+v&=\\frac{6x+2(vx)}{x} \\\\ x\\frac{\\mathrm{d}v}{\\mathrm{d}x}+v&=6+2v \\\\ x\\frac{\\mathrm{d}v}{\\mathrm{d}x}&=6+v \\\\ \\frac{1}{6+v}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}v}{\\mathrm{d}x}&=\\frac{1}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating both sides with respect to $x$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int\\frac{1}{6+v}\\,\\mathrm{d}v&=\\int\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ \\ln|v+6|&=\\ln|x|+C_1 \\\\ |v+6|&=e^{C_1}|x| \\\\ v+6&=Cx \\\\ v&=Cx-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the transformation $y=vx$, we get\n\n$$\nv=\\frac{y}{x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our solution, we finally obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y}{x}&=Cx-6 \\\\ y&=Cx^2-6x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe signed constant $C$ absorbs $e^{C_1}$. Division by $v+6$ excluded $v=-6$; restoring it permits $C=0$, giving $y=-6x$.\n\nThe solution is used on intervals where $x\\ne0$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572150 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2440da94-c49c-5b97-93a3-f1f305aaf546" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571599} {:answer/id #uuid "4dfdfa0c-df5d-578c-9e5a-030e1e19fe81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571679} {:answer/id #uuid "67441758-f1aa-545c-a9ad-7fa7f49bf8b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571715} {:answer/id #uuid "fb5ed5a3-55f9-5465-8515-fdd310345cd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571970} {:answer/id #uuid "fd4a6f37-6e13-59de-b1f0-4ae8dde2510a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571976}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186571599} :answer-field/id #uuid "5afb038d-0b31-5d55-8f54-c760388f6c4b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572027}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "87ece511-fd94-56a1-8fa2-055336c9156b" :question/math-academy-id "q-48848" :question/problem "Find the slope of the tangent to the curve $y=\\sqrt{3{x}^{2}+24}$ at the point where $x=-2.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the slope at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nWe use the chain rule in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet $u=3{x}^{2}+24.$ Then $y=\\sqrt{u}.$ Differentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=6x.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the two together gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}}\\cdot 6x \\\\  & =\\frac{3x}{\\sqrt{3{x}^{2}+24}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting  $x=-2,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=-2} & ={\\left(\\frac{3x}{\\sqrt{3{x}^{2}+24}}\\right)|}_{x=-2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-6)}{\\sqrt{3(-2)^{2}+24}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{6}{6} \\\\  & =-1\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572161 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "557cd32f-67a1-5f7d-8007-8e8dc4e07e92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2{({x}^{4}-2{x}^{3})}^{2}(4{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571691} {:answer/id #uuid "82e6a967-6c7d-5d88-8afe-9d6fff949b45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2({x}^{4}-2{x}^{3})(3{x}^{4}-6{x}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571760} {:answer/id #uuid "baf7a497-5f73-5773-889e-5e6f697822ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2({x}^{4}-2{x}^{3})(4{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571872} {:answer/id #uuid "caaa2a22-48c5-53fe-92ea-da472c888e6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2({x}^{4}-3{x}^{2})(4{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571901} {:answer/id #uuid "df3cad62-492d-5cb0-b710-42db57802071" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2({x}^{4}-2{x}^{3}){(4{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2})}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571938}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186571872} :answer-field/id #uuid "bbfbd138-787c-5944-9a48-89b79ecd75b3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572074}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "9d6e7296-3732-5370-89a1-2dbb983a355c" :question/math-academy-id "q-71951" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)={({x}^{4}-2{x}^{3})}^{2},$ find ${f}^{′}(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Let $g(x)={x}^{4}-2{x}^{3}$ and $f(g(x))=g(x)^{2}.$ \n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(g(x)) & =({g}^{2})^{′}=2g, \\\\ {g}^{′}(x) & =({x}^{4}-2{x}^{3})^{′}=4{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the chain rule, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={f}^{′}(g(x))\\cdot {g}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =2g\\cdot (4{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =2({x}^{4}-2{x}^{3})(4{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572194 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "096b9b79-42b4-5435-8d17-15938cf8083f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2+4x}{\\sqrt{x-{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571556} {:answer/id #uuid "528cbd11-0bdd-5861-899e-cfe78186526c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1-2x}{\\sqrt{(x-{x}^{2})^{3}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571688} {:answer/id #uuid "c895d3ba-c44d-57f2-8b2f-97e98d154d5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{1-2x}{\\sqrt{(x-{x}^{2})^{3}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571895} {:answer/id #uuid "de570552-69e0-5331-86f3-79143ee949ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{2+4x}{\\sqrt{(x-{x}^{2})^{3}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571936} {:answer/id #uuid "f88f7c0f-9d24-5617-aa25-c79abffb93e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2-4x}{\\sqrt{(x-{x}^{2})^{3}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571966}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186571966} :answer-field/id #uuid "c878ff99-495e-5613-8683-22e308482f13" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572080}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "e5c85892-5c29-5ec5-80d2-d47ed89d83b9" :question/math-academy-id "q-107298" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{′}(x)$ for $f(x)=-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{x-{x}^{2}}}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $g(x)=x-{x}^{2}$ and $f(g(x))=-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{g}}=-4{g}^{-1/2}.$ \n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(g(x)) & =-4({g}^{-1/2})^{′}=4\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{g}^{-3/2}=\\frac{2}{{g}^{3/2}}, \\\\ {g}^{′}(x) & =(x-{x}^{2})^{′}=1-2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the chain rule, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={f}^{′}(g(x))\\cdot {g}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{{g}^{3/2}}\\cdot (1-2x) \\\\  & =\\frac{2-4x}{\\sqrt{(x-{x}^{2})^{3}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573873 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ef97020-6eb8-5032-b55f-e4a453646fce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{2}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}-4{e}^{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573481} {:answer/id #uuid "73be6da6-0e94-54d9-8e28-80823daf499f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{{4}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}-{e}^{2x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573570} {:answer/id #uuid "961567fa-ad39-5dac-88d0-0e3ca76b9942" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{4}^{2x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}-2{e}^{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573619} {:answer/id #uuid "9dea4f6b-88de-50bf-9e41-7c205c1d30dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{4}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}-{e}^{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573629} {:answer/id #uuid "a75dd416-691c-506d-bff3-36ed676c1925" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}-{e}^{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573641}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573629} :answer-field/id #uuid "f535bffb-209d-5bbf-838b-5473917b087a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573860}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "149a14d8-d9d3-538d-9d01-436b9432ab15" :question/math-academy-id "q-2279" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int ({4}^{x}-{e}^{x})\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we combine the sum rule and our exponential rules to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int ({4}^{x}-{e}^{x})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {4}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x-\\int {e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{4}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}-{e}^{x}+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573895 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ae25c7f-44cb-5189-a1d0-644fd3146f1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\pi {e}^{2x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573451} {:answer/id #uuid "6bcaf640-1def-5f3f-84bc-9e753fd3979d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2{e}^{\\pi x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573555} {:answer/id #uuid "a8edbe47-2393-5cd6-b612-cfaa0aebf56b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\pi {e}^{x}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573643} {:answer/id #uuid "aa04a8fe-0d68-5cd3-84a1-8b67229f2002" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}{e}^{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573644} {:answer/id #uuid "d613ae8f-6382-57b9-800e-873ef80c1a41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2{e}^{x}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573708}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573644} :answer-field/id #uuid "4e609dbc-39c8-5f0a-b78b-cc260c4aa431" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573803}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "7338807d-a806-5642-ae5c-0fdf182692d4" :question/math-academy-id "q-113858" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{\\pi }{2}{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Factoring out the constant $\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and calculating the resulting integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\pi }{2}{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\int {e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}{e}^{x}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573944 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07836247-f997-5dfb-b77d-a88bd5744dd6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{{\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573432} {:answer/id #uuid "3c5b76da-5c79-5570-96fc-a1071399ac45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)}^{x}}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573497} {:answer/id #uuid "8096f421-e949-50b4-8f19-80003343c718" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3{\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)}^{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573592} {:answer/id #uuid "d2eb6285-99de-51bb-896a-d2849f05a9d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡3{\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)}^{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573702} {:answer/id #uuid "ec976108-75b3-594d-8698-a417623ef1c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡3{\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)}^{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573734}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573432} :answer-field/id #uuid "2cf68b31-cd10-5161-95fb-e446441e1ca2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573787}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "f3a89c81-1f21-57c4-8472-9cb98515b280" :question/math-academy-id "q-71910" :question/problem "Calculate $$\n\\displaystyle \\int {\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To compute the integral of a general exponential function, we just need to divide by the natural logarithm of the base of the exponential function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{{\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the laws of logarithms, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡1-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3 \\\\  & =0-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3 \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can simplify our final answer as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)}+C &=-\\frac{{\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186578821 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "377ccfc0-1263-5a65-9e54-437b028ff77c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}x^3+2x^2+x+e^x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186578358}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186578358} :answer-field/id #uuid "94d042fc-7530-5277-b11d-323323c45edf" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186578744}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "3e81fa55-2e11-5d7c-adb0-c91b70ee1041" :question/math-academy-id "q-167322" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int (g(x)+\\sqrt{h(x)})\\,\\text{d}x\\,=\n$${{field-1}}\n$+\\,C,\\,$ where $C$ is an arbitrary constant." :question/worked-solution "We combine the sum and the constant multiple rules, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (g(x)+\\sqrt{h(x)})\\text{d}x & =\\int (2{x}^{2}+4x+1+\\sqrt{{e}^{2x}})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (2{x}^{2}+4x+1+{e}^{x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x+4\\int x\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\,\\text{d}x+\\int {e}^{x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+4\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+x+{e}^{x}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{3}+2{x}^{2}+x+{e}^{x}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186578837 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7a57be08-0dbd-57eb-baa9-7dbfa44d370c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8x+8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186578464}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186578464} :answer-field/id #uuid "75b9845e-ad7e-59d5-bd52-917623fb75e5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186578731}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "69c70b64-ff8f-54e6-8fcc-bda6931079a9" :question/math-academy-id "q-167319" :question/problem "Given that $y=h(g(x)),$ calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=(${{field-1}}$){e}^{4{x}^{2}+8x+2}$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that $y$ is a composite function:\n\n$$\ny={e}^{s},\\,s=2g=2(2{x}^{2}+4x+1)=4{x}^{2}+8x+2.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}s}={e}^{s},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}x}=8x+8.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}s}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{s}\\cdot (8x+8) \\\\  & =(8x+8)\\,{e}^{4{x}^{2}+8x+2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186594665 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c14e8a2-231e-520a-9373-a71e0dd19e6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4t(t^2+3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186594381}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186594381} :answer-field/id #uuid "ec6431b2-e799-5371-92fe-40e4255fa0c2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186594657}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "016c901a-a8ed-57f7-ace0-713928705ac4" :question/math-academy-id "q-132770" :question/problem "$\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[({t}^{2}+3)^{2}]=\\,${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, let's define a function $h(t):$\n\n$$\nh(t)=({t}^{2}+3)^{2}\n$$\n\nTo differentiate this function, we use the chain rule. Let \n\n$$\ng(t)={t}^{2}+3,\\,h(g(t))=g(t)^{2}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating our functions, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(t) & =({t}^{2}+3)^{′}=2t, \\\\ {h}^{′}(g(t)) & =({g}^{2})^{′}=2g.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[({t}^{2}+3)^{2}] & ={h}^{′}(t) \\\\  & ={h}^{′}(g(t))\\cdot {g}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =2g\\cdot 2t \\\\  & =4t({t}^{2}+3).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186597617 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9590648e-813f-5f78-bbce-a306642395c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186597161} {:answer/id #uuid "6ec0b583-0f37-437e-9f53-f9413682363f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670961} {:answer/id #uuid "3be4d8a6-13d1-4307-8666-5cca126d0f67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186670962}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186597161} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a09aa38-da73-5206-b879-af0b3659206a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186597437}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "fb1316e2-9fcc-5550-830c-f3a945a647f2" :question/math-academy-id "q-342787" :question/problem "The slope of the tangent to the curve $y=\\sqrt{6x+1}$ at the point where $x=4$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the slope at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nWe use the chain rule in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet $u=6x+1.$ Then $y=\\sqrt{u}.$ Differentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}},\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=6.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the two together gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}}\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{2\\sqrt{6x+1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $x=4,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=4} & ={\\left(\\frac{6}{2\\sqrt{6x+1}}\\right)|}_{x=4} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{2\\sqrt{6(4)+1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{2\\sqrt{25}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186599198 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "44739b42-2bea-5e9b-8e09-51e916fde0c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$4\\sqrt{5}$ and $2\\sqrt{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186598822} {:answer/id #uuid "45173a72-7f31-50c4-b82a-4bc555a632b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$25$ and $9$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186598825} {:answer/id #uuid "55d94cf2-f20e-5890-b8d1-92a2a18a91d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$5$ and $3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186598852} {:answer/id #uuid "bc0e5d33-75fd-54ee-bd75-19007f555948" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$10$ and $6$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186599008} {:answer/id #uuid "db9d8e50-dc80-586a-8289-1b791b2428ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$2\\sqrt{5}$ and $2\\sqrt{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186599055}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186599008} :answer-field/id #uuid "28784dac-130d-50ff-a7dc-a4be2424124d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186599123}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "0c258564-3c20-5974-b831-5723221f599c" :question/math-academy-id "q-16453" :question/problem "What are the lengths of the major and minor axes of an ellipse with equation \n$\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}=1?$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have ${a}^{2}=25$ and ${b}^{2}=9.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=25,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{25}=5.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=9,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{9}=3.$\n\nSo the semi-major axis has length $a=5,$ and the semi-minor axis has length $b=3.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2a=2\\cdot 5=10,$ and the minor axis has length $2b=2\\cdot 3=6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186599252 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "330ca7aa-229f-55c6-a25d-cc9c0458c8c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}+\\frac{4{y}^{2}}{9}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186598791} {:answer/id #uuid "36ae38d5-c1a7-525c-81cd-621219b9ca12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186598801} {:answer/id #uuid "509da88f-4db9-5f0b-abe8-fdff7acb0ead" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{4{x}^{2}}{25}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186598842} {:answer/id #uuid "b395d2a5-637a-52a8-8e10-ba56845272a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{4{x}^{2}}{25}+\\frac{4{y}^{2}}{9}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186598995} {:answer/id #uuid "b3fe365d-58f2-5a52-bb5b-a2fbad55356e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186598996}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186598995} :answer-field/id #uuid "9cf11d5d-290d-5bae-8359-de14e8b96376" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186599168}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "c2e9daa0-47a0-517e-8133-871da3db599a" :question/math-academy-id "q-16457" :question/problem "![](images/19/1973e0499f9d6b756c1b2af3cc7ba0680631757dde93c5718e873c777b1dd5f0.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=\\frac{5}{2}$ and the vertical radius has length $b=\\frac{3}{2}.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{2.5}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{1.5}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{\\left(\\frac{5}{2}\\right)}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{\\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\left(\\frac{{5}^{2}}{{2}^{2}}\\right)}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{\\left(\\frac{{3}^{2}}{{2}^{2}}\\right)} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\left(\\frac{25}{4}\\right)}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{\\left(\\frac{9}{4}\\right)} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{4{x}^{2}}{25}+\\frac{4{y}^{2}}{9} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186599265 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "296d9194-b755-55fb-a920-e94099d3c308" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{1}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186598774} {:answer/id #uuid "3864cff4-57e5-51c4-98fc-8b92da615a99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186598805} {:answer/id #uuid "44b9d501-b27e-5517-ba29-49aaa49c85b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{1}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186598823} {:answer/id #uuid "b03bfd72-19a8-5191-9b62-fb303c9c7f59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{1}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186598988} {:answer/id #uuid "d7f50e7e-c861-5a6e-84be-4bed6310b486" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{1}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186599051}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186599051} :answer-field/id #uuid "7e613d2f-b159-5f7b-82c3-d670add737d8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186599159}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "f6e1505f-d95c-5726-a4ab-ec96ef6d05f8" :question/math-academy-id "q-115107" :question/problem "![](images/93/93483ece115081ec99c6a844c06b27b2927dba1e23f7ee9bd3da7d3fed924aff.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=2$ and the vertical radius has length $b=1.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{2}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{1}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{1} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186599774 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6846e12a-8c27-53f7-8cfe-bb746a3cf036" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$6$ and $3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186599475} {:answer/id #uuid "a6daa5a1-9f46-511d-99a0-5839ee6e3bbb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$12$ and $6$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186599556} {:answer/id #uuid "ae65ebc5-dcc2-5834-8f9b-6661ff467013" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$36$ and $9$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186599565} {:answer/id #uuid "e99d4f63-e744-5aa6-b59d-778174054f20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$24$ and $12$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186599642} {:answer/id #uuid "f0b1840a-a9bb-5845-addc-8fb4d2ddd66e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$12$ and $3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186599653}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186599556} :answer-field/id #uuid "ab8a5745-cdc4-594d-9a94-2eb77843cfae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186599737}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "0a7a3dbd-70b7-5aa3-861d-770dbf259134" :question/math-academy-id "q-115131" :question/problem "What are the lengths of the major and minor axes of an ellipse with equation \n$\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{36}=1?$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have ${a}^{2}=9$ and ${b}^{2}=36.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=9,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{9}=3.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=36,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{36}=6.$\n\nThus, the semi-major axis has length $b=6,$ and the semi-minor axis has length $a=3.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2b=2\\cdot 6=12,$ and the minor axis has length $2a=2\\cdot 3=6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186599781 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3059ff13-bee0-5604-921f-0e7150091621" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{49}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186599398} {:answer/id #uuid "59525aae-47bc-51bd-8b6e-5568cabc2862" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{7}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186599455} {:answer/id #uuid "595bbf9a-eb73-5c4c-ad57-6efce8a52e97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{14}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186599456} {:answer/id #uuid "d4607d17-5d8c-5d6b-b901-2c80beea4276" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{7}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186599611} {:answer/id #uuid "d60378b8-9add-5f16-bf03-a06da9a95ffa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{49}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186599614}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186599614} :answer-field/id #uuid "dd545641-b01d-5f8f-9b58-dad5d22ad2fc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186599756}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "29587bc0-bd52-5b45-9596-e43bc1394444" :question/math-academy-id "q-115128" :question/problem "![](images/78/78fad41612540c2741146a412da7cd5988180f192b177af7192bbf72d842030f.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=4$ and the vertical radius has length $b=7.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{4}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{7}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{49} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
